      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "An escrow agent plays a crucial role in real estate transactions by holding and disbursing funds from the buyer and seller to ensure the completion of the transaction. In the context of a Seattle house contract, the escrow agent typically holds the earnest money deposit (typically 1-3% of the purchase price) and any settlement funds (e.g., closing costs and repairs) until the deal is finalized. This helps prevent fraud and ensures that both parties fulfill their obligations.",
